You are working on "便利签看板", an Electron 28 + React 18 + Vite 5 desktop sticky note board app for Windows.

Read AGENTS.md in the project root for full project context before making changes.

Key rules:
- Main process: electron/main.js (Node.js) — windows, tray, IPC, auto-update
- Renderer: src/ (React, browser env) — UI components, call Electron via window.electronAPI
- Bridge: electron/preload.js — contextBridge whitelist
- Widget: electron/widget.html — standalone, self-contained HTML
- Styles: src/index.css — all CSS in one file, :root variables for theming
- Data: %APPDATA%/sticky-note-board/notes.json via notes:load/notes:save IPC
- IPC naming: module:action (e.g. notes:save, widget:click, update:available)
- CSS classes: kebab-case. Components: PascalCase. Comments: Chinese.
- No state management lib, no router, no CSS framework, no Tailwind.
- Frameless windows, drag via -webkit-app-region.
- Vite base must be './' for Electron file:// loading.
- Changes to electron/ require Electron restart; src/ hot-reloads via Vite.
- Local packaging: npm run pack (@electron/packager, stable).
- Release packaging: npm run dist (electron-builder, GitHub Actions).
- Release: npm version patch && git push --tags triggers GitHub Actions auto-build.
- Known issue: @electron/packager may omit semver/functions/prerelease.js from asar. setup-autostart.ps1 auto-fixes this.
- See CHANGELOG.md for version history.
